{"name":"Linnet","hex":"#c3bcb3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Linnet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from English, occasionally recorded since the 19th century."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Linnet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common linnet","blocks":[{"text":"The common linnet or Eurasian linnet is a small passerine bird of the finch family, Fringillidae. It derives its common name and the scientific name, Linaria, from its fondness for hemp seeds and flax seeds—flax being the English name of the plant from which linen is made."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Carduelis_cannabina_-England_-male-8.jpg/330px-Carduelis_cannabina_-England_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_linnet","wikidata":"Q27075852"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg/500px-2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg/1280px-2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg/500px-2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2017.07.06.-42-Wendisch_Rietz--Bluthaenfling-Weibchen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/LinariaCannabinaIUCN2019_2.png/500px-LinariaCannabinaIUCN2019_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p